{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01JPXXi3nia9t2om8FWmxvGq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed this run:\n\n**`answers/07-005-gpt-based-api-calls-cost-efficient-under-heavy-load.md`** — Q5: GPT-based API calls cost-efficient under heavy load?\n\nKey content:\n- **7-layer efficiency stack**: (1) semantic cache (cosine ≥0.93, 25-35% hit rate, GPTCache/Redis), (2) exact cache for deterministic calls, (3) prompt compression via LLMLingua 2-5×, (4) model tiering 80% GPT-4o-mini / 20% GPT-4o (84% cost cut on those calls), (5) prefix caching (50-90% discount on static system prompt tokens — OpenAI Nov 2024), (6) Batch API for async workloads (50% discount, 24h SLA), (7) rate-limit management (exponential backoff + jitter, proactive quota provisioning)\n- **Before/after table**: naive $10,500/day → ~$630/day with all layers (~94% reduction)\n- **Key pitfalls**: saying \"add caching\" without specifying threshold/TTL; ignoring output token cost (4-10× more expensive than input); not mentioning prefix caching (free optimization, just prompt ordering)\n\n**Up next (Q6):** Quantization and model distillation for inference?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":76539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":288,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4a04d0f-6236-4dfa-b255-e92dc6f71818","uuid":"8bab8483-b79c-4c15-8a6f-373accce7393"}
